.\" Outsider — Man Page
.TH OUS 1 "2026-08-22" "ous 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ous \- Outsider: the Cudane package builder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ous
.RI [ options ]
.I MANIFEST OUTPUT_DIR
.br
.B ous
.RB [ \-a | \-\-archive ]
.I SRC OUT.xcs
.br
.B ous
.RB [ \-x | \-\-extract ]
.I PACKAGE.xcs|DIR ROOT
.br
.B ous
.RB [ \-i | \-\-inspect ]
.I PACKAGE.xcs
.br
.B ous \-\-sort
.I DIR ARCH
.br
.B ous \-\-validate
.I INDEX.json DIR
.br
.B ous \-\-checksum
.I INDEX.json DIR
.RB [ \-\-base\-url
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-arch
.IR ARCH ]
.br
.B ous \-\-source
.I INDEX.json
.RB [ \-\-base\-url
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-arch
.IR ARCH ]
.br
.B ous
.RB [ \-g | \-\-sign ]
.I INDEX.json DIR
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR KEYID ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ous
builds and packages Cudane software into self-extracting archives (.xcs), and
provides build-aware prompts, plugins, themes, and TUIs via the shared cps
engine.
.br
It reads a JSON manifest describing the build, fetches sources, builds each
package, stages the output, and wraps it as a distributable archive with a
detached SHA-256 sidecar file.
.SH BUILD OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-manifest \fIFILE\fR
Path to the manifest.json describing the packages to build.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIDIR\fR
Directory that receives the built .xcs archives.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-target \fIARCH\fR
Target architecture triple (e.g. x86_64-unknown-linux-musl).
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-auto
Disable automatic build/install behaviors.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Overwrite existing .xcs packages; forces re-running the archive/hash/metadata
steps even when a resume state marks them complete.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-clean
Clean the package workspace before building.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-parallel
Process manifest entries in parallel.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs \fINUM\fR
Maximum number of parallel jobs/workers.
.TP
.B \-z, \-\-zstd\-level \fINUM\fR
zstd compression level, 1–22 (default: 3).
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-strict
Fail when libraries cannot be resolved to a providing package.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error output.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Assume "yes" for all confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-project \fIDIR\fR
Use DIR as the project workspace root instead of the current directory.
.SH STANDALONE COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-archive \fISRC\fR \fIOUT.xcs\fR
Archive directory SRC into an .xcs tar+zstd archive.
.TP
.B \-x, \-\-extract \fIPACKAGE\fR \fIROOT\fR
Extract an .xcs package (or every *.xcs inside a directory) into rootfs ROOT.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-write \fISRC\fR \fIDEST\fR
Generate metadata.json for a manually constructed package tree.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-inspect \fIPACKAGE.xcs\fR
Show size, timestamps, and integrity of a package; verifies against the
detached \fIPACKAGE.sha256\fR sidecar when present.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-hash\-type \fITYPE\fR
Checksum algorithm: sha256 (default), sha1 or md5.
.SH REPOSITORY COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-sort \fIDIR\fR \fIARCH\fR
Sort .xcs files into pool/\fIARCH\fR/\fIname\fR/ layout. Refuses to overwrite
an existing destination unless \fB\-\-force\fR is given or confirmed.
.TP
.B \-\-validate \fIINDEX.json\fR \fIDIR\fR
Check index/package consistency; exits non-zero on problems.
.TP
.B \-\-checksum \fIINDEX.json\fR \fIDIR\fR
Add SHA-256 sums and rewritten source URLs to the index.
.TP
.B \-\-source \fIINDEX.json\fR
Rewrite source URLs in the index to pool paths.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-sign \fIINDEX.json\fR \fIDIR\fR
GPG-detach-sign the index and every .xcs package.
.TP
.B \-\-base\-url \fIURL\fR, \fB\-\-arch \fIARCH\fR, \fB\-\-key \fIKEYID\fR
Repository modifiers consumed by the preceding commands; they may appear
before or after the command they modify.
.SH PLUGIN / THEME / TUI
.TP
.B \-\-plugin \fIlist|run|reload\fR ...
List, run (\fIname func [args...]\fR) or reload cps plugins.
.TP
.B \-\-theme \fIlist|apply\fR ...
List or apply cps themes.
.TP
.B \-\-tui \fIlist|run\fR ...
List or run cps TUI apps.
.PP
Registering and unregistering plugins/themes/TUIs from the CLI is not
supported: descriptors are managed by editing the \fIp.desc\fR / \fIt.desc\fR
files directly.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OUS_TARGET, OUS_JOBS, OUS_PARALLEL, OUS_FORCE, OUS_CLEAN, OUS_NO_AUTO,
.B OUS_STRICT, OUS_DEBUG, OUS_QUIET, OUS_ASSUME_YES, OUS_ZSTD_LEVEL,
.B OUS_HASH_TYPE, OUS_PROJECT_WORKSPACE
Equivalent to the like-named command line options; flags take precedence.
.TP
.B CUDANE_REPO_URL, CUDANE_TARGET
Fallback base URL / architecture for repository commands.
.TP
.B GPG_KEY_ID
Fallback signing key for \fB--sign\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I manifest.json
JSON build manifest consumed by
.BR ous .
.TP
.I ous.toml
Optional per-project configuration (see config documentation); values are
exposed through the OUS_* environment unless overridden by CLI flags.
.TP
.I PACKAGE.xcs.sha256
Detached SHA-256 sidecar written next to every packaged archive.
.TP
.I p.desc , t.desc
Plugin and theme/TUI descriptor files managed by cps.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on operational failure (including unconfirmed prompts and
duplicate manifest entries); 2 when \fB--hash-type\fR receives an unknown
algorithm; \fB--validate\fR exits with the number of problems found (capped
at 255).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cps (1)
